# ENTERPRISE ERP / SAP-STYLE SOFTWARE — COMPLETE DEPARTMENT, FORM, REPORT, WORKFLOW & INTEGRATION BLUEPRINT

## 1. MAIN OBJECTIVE

Build a complete enterprise-level ERP software inspired by SAP S/4HANA, SAP Business One, Odoo, Microsoft Dynamics 365 and Oracle ERP.

This software must support small businesses, medium businesses, large enterprises, manufacturing factories, trading companies, distributors, import/export companies, schools, colleges, universities, hospitals, clinics, construction companies, solar companies, textile industries, food industries, retail businesses, service companies and other business categories.

The system must not be a basic accounting or inventory application. It must be a fully integrated, modular ERP platform.

### Mandatory development rules

- Every department must have its own independent structure.
- Every department must have its own Definition, Master Data, Submodules, Forms, Reports, Dashboard, Settings and Approval Workflow.
- Every individual form must have its own unique fields according to its actual business purpose.
- Every individual report must have its own specific columns, filters, calculations and output format.
- Do not use the same generic form structure for all departments.
- Do not use the same generic reports in different departments.
- All forms and reports must open in separate professional popup windows or modal screens.
- Every transaction must have a unique automatically generated document number.
- All departments must be connected through an integrated database and workflow engine.
- Approved transactions must automatically trigger the next required process wherever applicable.
- The system must maintain complete audit history, user permissions and approval records.
- The system must support configurable workflows according to business category, company size and management requirements.

